From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Archit Gupta <archit@accelbread.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:57:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Prevent GLib signal-list corruption from PGTK nonlocal exits

Lisp nonlocal exits from GTK callbacks bypass GLib's cleanup of its
stack-allocated Emission entries. Subsequent signal emissions can follow
those dangling entries and segfault.

This was observed from a hung Emacs core dump, though root cause is unknown.
---
 src/pgtkim.c   |  12 ++---
 src/pgtkterm.c | 127 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 src/pgtkterm.h |   1 +
 3 files changed, 106 insertions(+), 34 deletions(-)

